From e886444223965abe98b324c7933e59091d6d01f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:35:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] nfsd: leave the umask to the VFS in NFSv4 creates

Since commit 5aa8fd9cea2e ("fs: add a new SB_I_NOUMASK flag"), an NFSv4
mount sets SB_I_NOUMASK instead of SB_POSIXACL, which tells the VFS to
leave the umask to the filesystem. nfsd only looks at IS_POSIXACL(), so
when an NFSv4.2 mount is re-exported it strips the umask before
forwarding the create, and a default ACL on the directory underneath can
no longer override it.

nfsd does not need to strip it at all: vfs_create(), vfs_mkdir(),
vfs_mknod() and dentry_create() go through vfs_prepare_mode(), which
calls mode_strip_umask() with the same current_umask(), and
nfsd_create_setattr() drops ATTR_MODE afterwards. This also lets
S_ISGID be stripped before S_IXGRP goes, the order vfs_prepare_mode()
wants. On tmpfs without POSIX ACLs, a caller outside the directory's
group creating 02775 under umask 010 used to get 2765 and now gets 0765.

With tmpfs exported, mounted over NFSv4.2, re-exported and mounted
again, and "setfacl -d -m u::rwx,g::rwx,o::rwx" on the directory, umask
077 creates files as 0600 and directories as 0700, where 0666 and 0777
are expected. It passes on 84d2b696236c, the parent of 5aa8fd9cea2e, and
fails on 5aa8fd9cea2e. With this patch it passes on nfsd-testing
d692f252c52b, and pynfs reports LOCK24 and CSESS22 as it does without.

Fixes: 5aa8fd9cea2e ("fs: add a new SB_I_NOUMASK flag")
Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
---
 fs/nfsd/nfs4proc.c | 3 ---
 fs/nfsd/vfs.c      | 3 ---
 2 files changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/nfsd/nfs4proc.c b/fs/nfsd/nfs4proc.c
index 03ea955f1..090518760 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/nfs4proc.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/nfs4proc.c
@@ -359,9 +359,6 @@ nfsd4_create_file(struct svc_rqst *rqstp, struct svc_fh *fhp,
 			dput(child);
 	}
 
-	if (!IS_POSIXACL(d_inode(parent.dentry)))
-		iap->ia_mode &= ~current_umask();
-
 	/*
 	 * For the EXCLUSIVE modes we do our own uniqueness tests
 	 * so don't want O_EXCL.
diff --git a/fs/nfsd/vfs.c b/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
index 02df2ff02..c6a71fb84 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
@@ -2034,9 +2034,6 @@ nfsd_create_locked(struct svc_rqst *rqstp, struct svc_fh *fhp,
 		iap->ia_mode = 0;
 	iap->ia_mode = (iap->ia_mode & S_IALLUGO) | type;
 
-	if (!IS_POSIXACL(dirp))
-		iap->ia_mode &= ~current_umask();
-
 	err = 0;
 	switch (type) {
 	case S_IFREG:
